# DTF tier manifest: http-edge-limits  (artifact-keeper#4665, #4672, #4664, #4671, #4673; all 1.11.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem + profiles/limits.http-edge.yml, which sets
# MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=1048576 and HTTP_HEADER_READ_TIMEOUT_SECS=5 so the oracle can
# cross both in a few seconds and a few KiB. The rate limiter stays ON (the
# compose default, set explicitly here): the release gate deploys with it
# OFF, so the login limiter's headers (#4664) have never been exercised there.
#
# THE FIXES (1.11.1; red on 1.11.0)
#   #4665 (PR #4685): axum::serve set no hyper timer, so a client that sent a
#         partial request head, or nothing, held its socket indefinitely. The
#         new accept loop closes it after HTTP_HEADER_READ_TIMEOUT_SECS and
#         counts it in ak_http_header_read_timeouts_total.
#   #4672 (PR #4682): POST /v2/<name>/blobs/uploads/ (session create with a
#         body, and the monolithic ?digest= form) streamed the body until it
#         crossed MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE; a client that declared more than it sent
#         waited for the stall watchdog. The declared length is now checked
#         first, as PATCH already did.
#   #4664 (PR #4686): the outer API limiter overwrote the login limiter's
#         429 headers with its own X-RateLimit-Limit: 10000.
#   #4671 (PR #4684): POST /api/v1/plugins/install/local resolved the path on
#         the server and answered 500 (existing path) or 400 (missing); it is
#         now a fixed 501 NOT_IMPLEMENTED.
#   #4673 (PR #4682): a .vsix with '..', absolute, backslash-rooted or
#         drive-qualified entry names was stored and served verbatim.
#
# The oracle drives the raw-socket cases with fixtures/edge_probe.py (stdlib
# python, every wait bounded, so a red backend fails a case instead of
# hanging the tier).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem limits.http-edge"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="true"
